DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions return a simple checksum of the ELF object described by
     their argument _e_l_f.  The checksum is computed in way that allows its
     value to remain unchanged in presence of modifications to the ELF object
     by utilities like strip(1).

     Function eellff3322__cchheecckkssuumm() returns a checksum for an ELF descriptor _e_l_f of
     class ELFCLASS32.

     Function eellff6644__cchheecckkssuumm() returns a checksum for an ELF descriptor _e_l_f of
     class ELFCLASS64.

     Function ggeellff__cchheecckkssuumm() provides a class-independent way retrieving the
     checksum for ELF object _e_l_f.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     These functions return the checksum of the ELF object, or zero in case an
     error was encountered.

EERRRROORRSS
     These functions may fail with the following errors:

     [ELF_E_ARGUMENT]  Argument _e_l_f was NULL.

     [ELF_E_ARGUMENT]  Argument _e_l_f was not a descriptor for an ELF file.

     [ELF_E_ARGUMENT]  The ELF descriptor _e_l_f was not opened for reading or
                       updating.

     [ELF_E_CLASS]     For functions eellff3322__cchheecckkssuumm() and eellff6644__cchheecckkssuumm(),
                       ELF descriptor _e_l_f did not match the class of the
                       called function.

     [ELF_E_HEADER]    The ELF object specified by argument _e_l_f had a mal‐
                       formed executable header.

     [ELF_E_RESOURCE]  An out of memory condition was detected during process‐
                       ing.

     [ELF_E_SECTION]   The ELF object specified by argument _e_l_f contained a
                       section with a malformed section header.

     [ELF_E_VERSION]   The ELF object was of an unsupported version.

